  "title": "mirrors",
  "heading": "Mirrors",
  "description": "Mirrors in late twentieth-century painting.",
  "source_encoding": "utf-8",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Mirrors (Absence.)",
      "links": [],
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The perfect monochrome is a surface without any\nmarks: uniform, textureless, polished: a mirror.\n\n\"Nothing\" turns into \"anything\": the perfect monochrome throws the world back at the spectator.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "(Tautology.)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The mirror only reflects what is already there.\n\n\nIt can show anything, but it cannot make a difference.\n\nIt says: x = x.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "(Narcissism.)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The only exception is the thing that cannot be duplicated: the subject.\n\nThe mirror returns the gaze of the observer. The subject becomes an object.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "(Fun.)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A mirror surface with a non-uniform\norientation presents a multiplied, fragmented and/or distorted image\nof the world and the viewer. Automated cubism becomes a joke.",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "(Infinity.)",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A closed optical loop between two or more mirrors\nmultiplies an image ad infinitum.\n\nPistoletto's \"Metrocubo d'Infinito\" implements the thought experiment: What if there is no\ninput image?",
      "links": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Les Expositions des Arts Incohérents",
      "links": [],
      "level": 3
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Detouche & Melandri: Mirror entitled \"Quelques\nspecimens des animaux embarqués par Noé dans son\narche.\" (One of the exhibits in the \"Musée semitique\net semi-toc\", 1883.)\n\n\n\nMirror entitled \"Une bonne bille\". [Date? Author?]\n\n\n\nMirror entitled \"Portrait de tout le monde – cent francs\nà qui ne se reconnaît pas\", 1889. [Author?]",
      "links": []
    },
